                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cc9d3475-382b-3f9d-917b-38101a68e588",
                        "entry_id": "e1a373b9-06c8-3edb-a07a-38caee1e0d09",
                        "glosses": [
                            "etwas, das dem Anblick oder Ansehen einer Sache abträglich ist"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b55e3f7c-a2a1-4a81-b13e-ac0008c8a4e7",
                                "sense_id": "cc9d3475-382b-3f9d-917b-38101a68e588",
                                "text": "„Manchen ist er ein Kultautor, ein Teil der Avantgarde, anderen indes zu vulgär, ein Schandfleck der argentinischen Literatur.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d06e047-1526-4634-93e0-2310d44ab71c",
                                "sense_id": "cc9d3475-382b-3f9d-917b-38101a68e588",
                                "text": "„Als Schandfleck galt vielen das Bauwerk, das damals das höchste der Welt war.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1cd453e4-1eb0-4565-a1ed-e2b191ff4432",
                        "source_entry_id": "e1a373b9-06c8-3edb-a07a-38caee1e0d09",
                        "source_sense_id": "cc9d3475-382b-3f9d-917b-38101a68e588",
                        "source_sense_description": "etwas, das dem Anblick oder Ansehen einer Sache abträglich ist",
                        "target_lang_word": "blemish",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "blemish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8a4a584-5c4f-3821-a4cc-b6e9a4b2e71d",
                                        "entry_id": "0a695418-e564-34b9-8f4d-797bfae8015b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small flaw which spoils the appearance of something, a stain, a spot."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42aeb560-c2b8-4857-a733-258e86602dbe",
                                                "sense_id": "c8a4a584-5c4f-3821-a4cc-b6e9a4b2e71d",
                                                "text": "Ye shall offer at your own will a male without blemish, of the beeves, of the sheep, or of the goats."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d15ff5d4-8078-40c2-a75e-924dc06b4f7c",
                                                "sense_id": "c8a4a584-5c4f-3821-a4cc-b6e9a4b2e71d",
                                                "text": "Any foot shape deviating from this model is conceived as a blemish, and the animal is unclean."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a79ba82-8568-49c9-8c53-2c568356a13d",
                                                "sense_id": "c8a4a584-5c4f-3821-a4cc-b6e9a4b2e71d",
                                                "text": "There are a very large number of types of blemish and the smallest blemish visible to a human can be surprisingly small, for example less than 10μm deep, which may be on the surface of a heavily embossed tile."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca12c150-42c2-47e6-bb1d-7fe0300f14ca",
                                                "sense_id": "c8a4a584-5c4f-3821-a4cc-b6e9a4b2e71d",
                                                "text": "It comes as a surprise to some people, but blemishes can strike at any age. To minimize the appearance of facial blemishes or pimples, use a concealer with a dry texture; it will cling to the blemish better, last throughout the day, and not irritate the skin or initiate more breakouts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "211ec2ef-b7f3-3192-b98b-83ffea62b383",
                                        "entry_id": "0a695418-e564-34b9-8f4d-797bfae8015b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A moral defect; a character flaw."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "993468c4-1534-4d05-a47a-1e03cd8ba7cb",
                                                "sense_id": "211ec2ef-b7f3-3192-b98b-83ffea62b383",
                                                "text": "As piety is the peculiar ornament of old people, so the want of it is a peculiar blemish in their character."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f22e4293-74ea-4f56-be37-41c5399b25bc",
                                                "sense_id": "211ec2ef-b7f3-3192-b98b-83ffea62b383",
                                                "text": "The processes of categorization, stereotyping, discrimination, and self-fulfilling prophecy can also apply to stigmas based on blemishes of individual character."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44787fcd-8bdc-485e-a755-c742e44d51cf",
                                                "sense_id": "211ec2ef-b7f3-3192-b98b-83ffea62b383",
                                                "text": "There is no reason to think that the enlivening possible blemish was his hypocritical show of repentance, since there are so many other candidate blemishes to choose among."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "blemish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a9f8e0e-57a1-3953-a954-421d598bcdd9",
                                        "entry_id": "f257e01a-6806-341b-ae8e-d3d3db6c4334",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To spoil the appearance of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d56dfba-59d0-4b93-9410-1b983c38a591",
                                                "sense_id": "6a9f8e0e-57a1-3953-a954-421d598bcdd9",
                                                "text": "we see ordinarie examples by this licence which wonderfully blemisheth the authoritie and lustre of our law, never to stay upon one sentence, but to run from one to another judge, to decide one same case."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8e5e71b-35b6-43bb-9b56-4ee53fd4d184",
                                                "sense_id": "6a9f8e0e-57a1-3953-a954-421d598bcdd9",
                                                "text": "Generally, varieties in current use for processing are resilient, if not wholly resistant to blemishing diseases and disorders."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bfc3792d-424c-488a-a2c0-d38f88f61608",
                                                "sense_id": "6a9f8e0e-57a1-3953-a954-421d598bcdd9",
                                                "text": "I mean it reaches a point of ridiculousness in some regards, and one′s seen actually many good schemes here in San Francisco, for example, that have been blemished by an overly strict adherence to codes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0fdf66ad-2f9a-3089-aab1-70c3cff05147",
                                        "entry_id": "f257e01a-6806-341b-ae8e-d3d3db6c4334",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To tarnish (reputation, character, etc.); to defame."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d84842a5-6130-46b3-af84-0e52bc9786c1",
                                                "sense_id": "0fdf66ad-2f9a-3089-aab1-70c3cff05147",
                                                "text": "There had nothing passed betwixt us that might blemish reputation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2688ff0d-8296-479d-8044-b38ab63cce0d",
                        "source_entry_id": "e1a373b9-06c8-3edb-a07a-38caee1e0d09",
                        "source_sense_id": "cc9d3475-382b-3f9d-917b-38101a68e588",
                        "source_sense_description": "etwas, das dem Anblick oder Ansehen einer Sache abträglich ist",
                        "target_lang_word": "disgrace",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "disgrace",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af9f5d1c-214c-3f41-8c98-ba33b4a6b5be",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of being out of favor; loss of favor, regard, or respect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbc174b0-9d1e-4575-ac38-d9b3727b12c9",
                                                "sense_id": "af9f5d1c-214c-3f41-8c98-ba33b4a6b5be",
                                                "text": "I heare / Macduffe liues in diſgrace. Sir, can you tell / Where he beſtowes himſelfe?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6be99cd5-8000-39e5-aab9-78c3cfd109e1",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being dishonored, or covered with shame."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7756053a-8f4a-47b8-a6dc-35ce986c9d1f",
                                                "sense_id": "6be99cd5-8000-39e5-aab9-78c3cfd109e1",
                                                "text": "Now she lives in disgrace."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "161ed4fb-fdb4-3973-bd91-75d3def376ac",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something which brings dishonor; the cause of reproach or shame; great discredit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6366a8e0-9952-49d6-826e-46e7372d03ac",
                                                "sense_id": "161ed4fb-fdb4-3973-bd91-75d3def376ac",
                                                "text": "His behaviour at the party was a total disgrace! He was leeching on all the ladies, and insulting the men."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0e8ca50-9b33-4a8d-8471-0825a5e950d1",
                                                "sense_id": "161ed4fb-fdb4-3973-bd91-75d3def376ac",
                                                "text": "Practice and whipping were alike unavailing, and Epps, satisfied of it at last, swore I was a disgrace—that I was not fit to associate with a cotton-picking \"nigger\"—that I could not pick enough in a day to pay the trouble of weighing it, and that I should go into the cotton field no more."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74fcdf24-767f-3906-890a-83d77428e0ad",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act of unkindness; a disfavor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "358e13b3-720c-4406-b42c-04b97bbfb423",
                                                "sense_id": "74fcdf24-767f-3906-890a-83d77428e0ad",
                                                "text": "As for the pulling of them [ambitious men] downe, if the Affaires require it, and that it may not be done with ſafety ſuddainly, the onely Way is, the Enterchange, continually of Fauours, and Diſgraces, whereby they may not know, what to expect; And be, as it were, in a Wood."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "disgrace",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e20ef1d8-7040-3dc1-b0a5-da0a9fb4735f",
                                        "entry_id": "3de008e8-961c-3a15-a0c5-566717b3bb8c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put someone or something out of favor; to bring shame or ignominy upon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e07fe5c7-a9db-4a30-a640-26c42383455e",
                                                "sense_id": "e20ef1d8-7040-3dc1-b0a5-da0a9fb4735f",
                                                "text": "[…] some families renounced the use of a certain praenomen which had been disgraced by one of their name […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
